      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} The most easily seen for me to note would be the Trans Academy events. In-client, they are all marked as featured events whilst on the website, some are not. In the attached screenshots below, you can just look at all of the Wednesdays of the month and see the issue but there are a variety of other things there on the website that are mislabeled until you actually click on the event and see that they are featured.\n\nAlso, not sure if this is actually relevant but when I was speaking to some more tech literate friends about what the issue is, they said there's a decent possibility of some error occuring between how the api endpoints fetch content for the calendar for groups that you are in and then just the Vrchat featured events. Or rather, how that information is being portrayed to the user on the website. As this seems to be an issue if you are in a group and also that group is featured, so some problem occurs when it tries to display it as just a regular group event rather than something that should be properly tagged as a featured event.\n\nMaybe that's all conjecture though, but that's all the info I got for ya.",
